Z||000014||Songman||06-16-2001||04:10 PM||||Not sure how many are still on the road. I know a lot of them that I have seen are fakes these days.<P>I got the paperwork from Pontiac Historical on mine. The Ram Air IV with 4-speed made it 1 of 237.<P>Not sure about the numbers on the Firebird. It is just a stock 350 car. But it did come with a/c, power windows, power top and a hood tach. What I couldn't believe was that someone got all of that and didn't opt for power disc brakes.<P>I'm a Pontiac man from way back! I'll try to get some pictures of my 66 Star Chief Executive sometime, and the 455 Bonny. I found a guy that will sell me a 67 2+2 convertible for $1000! I haven't seen it yet, but he says it has 3x2s and a 4-speed!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 06-16-2001).]||||reg||1
